Geodata in course packages (course.json, preview and map images, 3D scenes) is derived from open
government and community data under their own licences, which require attribution. Each course lists
its sources in course.json ("attribution") and the app shows them. Sources used so far:

- Switzerland: © swisstopo (swissALTI3D, SWISSIMAGE, swissBUILDINGS3D 3.0, swissSURFACE3D Raster,
  swissTLM3D), Open Government Data (free use with attribution)
- Berlin: Geoportal Berlin (TrueOrthophotos 2025, DGM1, LoD2 buildings, bDOM), Datenlizenz Deutschland –
  Zero – 2.0
- Brandenburg: © GeoBasis-DE/LGB (DGM1, DOP20), Datenlizenz Deutschland – Namensnennung – 2.0
- Hamburg: Freie und Hansestadt Hamburg, Landesbetrieb Geoinformation und Vermessung (LGV),
  Datenlizenz Deutschland – Namensnennung – 2.0 (DOP 2024, DGM1 2022, bDOM 2022, LoD2-DE 2026)
- Poland: Główny Urząd Geodezji i Kartografii (GUGiK, geoportal.gov.pl) – Ortofotomapa, NMT/NMPT, BDOT10k;
  data of the state geodetic and cartographic resource, made available free of charge (art. 40a(2)(1)
  of the Polish Geodetic and Cartographic Law), processed
- Austria: BEV – Bundesamt für Eich- und Vermessungswesen (ALS-Höhenraster DTM/DSM 1 m), CC BY 4.0
  (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/), modified; orthophotos: basemap.at, CC BY 4.0, modified
- USA: U.S. Geological Survey, 3D Elevation Program (3DEP) – 1 m DEM and lidar point cloud (public domain),
  modified; orthophotos: MassGIS (Bureau of Geographic Information), Commonwealth of Massachusetts, modified
- Norway: © Kartverket, Høydedata DTM1 and DOM1 1 m (hoydedata.no), CC BY 4.0
  (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/), modified; ground imagery synthetic from Copernicus Sentinel-2 and OSM
- Brazil (Rio de Janeiro): buildings Instituto Pereira Passos (IPP), Prefeitura da Cidade do Rio de Janeiro –
  Edificações (2013), CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/), modified
- Argentina (Tigre): building footprints in part from Microsoft Global ML Building Footprints, CDLA Permissive 2.0
  (https://cdla.dev/permissive-2-0/)
- Copernicus DEM GLO-30: produced using Copernicus WorldDEM-30 © DLR e.V. 2010-2014 and © Airbus Defence and
  Space GmbH 2014-2018 provided under COPERNICUS by the European Union and ESA; all rights reserved.
  The organisations in charge of the Copernicus programme by law or by delegation do not incur any liability
  for any use of the Copernicus WorldDEM-30.
- Water areas, piers and bridges: © OpenStreetMap contributors, Open Database License (ODbL),
  https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright. Where OSM data is modified (e.g. building heights, water areas),
  the method is the open source code in tools/coursebuilder (ODbL 4.6).

Courses added later name further sources in their course.json (e.g. Environment Agency (OGL v3),
Kartverket (Høydedata DTM1/DOM1, CC BY 4.0, "© Kartverket", modified), IGN (Licence Ouverte 2.0), GSI and Project PLATEAU (CC BY 4.0 compatible),
Copernicus Sentinel-2).

Files under courses/ (course.json, preview images, mini maps, overviews) and the course scenes contain or are
derived from the geodata above and are licensed under the respective source licences, not under Apache-2.0.
German sources under dl-de/by-2-0 are used with modifications ("Daten geändert").

The raw geodata itself is not part of this repository; tools/coursebuilder downloads it from the
official services.

Avatar skin tones (App/RowCoach/Resources/appearance.json, "skinTones") are the ten swatch colours of the
Monk Skin Tone Scale by Dr. Ellis Monk, licensed under CC BY 4.0
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/; https://skintone.google). The display names are our own.

Virtual participants (App/RowCoach/Resources/virtual-rowers-v1.bin, generated by
App/RowCoachKit/Sources/RowCoachKit/VirtualRowers/) are made-up rowers; no real person is reproduced. Their first
names come from "popular-names-by-country-dataset" by sigpwned (https://github.com/sigpwned/popular-names-by-country-dataset,
commit eb62e13), dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0, itself compiled from the Wikipedia lists of most
popular given names (July 2023); Swedish names from Skatteverket, name statistics for newborns 2024. Their
performance distribution follows the public Concept2 RowErg 2000 m rankings 2025 (aggregate quantiles only).
